ction><section><h2>Charleston tile passing</h2><p>The Charleston is a series of tile exchanges before normal play. The sequence and optional passes should follow the rules adopted by your group.</p></section><section><h2>Jokers have limits</h2><p>Jokers can substitute in eligible groups but not everywhere. In particular, a joker cannot simply replace any tile in any hand. Consult the current rules for exact restrictions and exchanges.</p></section><section><h2>Exposed and concealed hands</h2><p>Calling a discard can reveal tiles in an exposed grouping. Some card hands must remain concealed, so calls may be restricted.</p></section><section><h2>Scoring and etiquette</h2><p>Scoring depends on the hand and the rules in use. Agree on table etiquette, mistaken exposures and dispute handling before a beginner game.</p></section><aside><strong>A note on official rules</strong><p>This is an independent educational overview, not a substitute for the current official National Mah Jongg League card or rules. We do not reproduce copyrighted annual card patterns.</p></aside><h2>Keep exploring</h2><div class="related"><a href="/">a →</a><a href="S">t →</a><a href="/">a →</a><a href="T">i →</a><a href="/#tools">Free tools →</a></div></main><footer>© {new Date().getFullYear()} My Mahjong Era · Independent American Mahjong learning and lifestyle</footer></body></html>